---
import MilloraPrivacy from "../../components/MilloraPrivacy.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy — VCode" description="How VCode handles data on the website and in technology blog comments." lang="en" path="/en/privacy/" alternatePath="/soukromi/">
  <article class="guide">
    <a class="back-link" href="/en/">← VCode</a>
    <header><p class="kicker">Privacy</p><h1>Only the data the service needs.</h1><p>You can read the website without an account. We process information needed for support, comments and aggregate traffic measurement on the public website.</p></header>
    <div class="guide-body">
      <h2>Blog comments</h2><p>For a comment, we store the chosen display name, text, time and technical data needed to protect the discussion. Email is optional and stored only as a one-way hash. We protect the IP address in the same way and never display it publicly.</p>
      <h2>Moderation</h2><p>Comment text may be assessed automatically by OpenAI to detect harmful or illegal content. If automated review is unavailable or uncertain, the comment waits for manual review. We do not publish comments identified as spam.</p>
      <h2>Retention</h2><p>Pending, rejected and spam comments are deleted within 90 days. Published comments remain with the article until you ask us to remove them or the discussion no longer serves its purpose.</p>
      <h2>Your requests</h2><p>To request correction or removal, contact <a href="mailto:podpora@zeleznalady.cz"><strong>podpora@zeleznalady.cz</strong></a>. Include the article address, display name and approximate submission time; never send passwords or other sensitive information.</p>

      <h2>Traffic on public websites</h2><p>We use Umami analytics hosted on our own server to improve our public websites. We measure public pages visited, visits, basic browser and device information, the referring domain, and clicks to the App Store or an email contact. Campaign parameters are limited to source, channel and campaign labels. Other URL parameters and fragments are not sent to analytics.</p><p>Analytics does not use tracking cookies or a visitor's signed-in identity. The IP address is temporarily processed to estimate visitors; it is not stored in readable form in the analytics database. The identifier used for this estimate changes daily. Statistics may include an approximate country and device type. We do not record screens or sessions, form contents, comments or private application activity. We respect Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals.</p><p>Statistics are accessible only to authorized people after sign-in. Detailed analytics records are retained for no more than 180 days. Operational and security server logs are separate from these analytics records.</p>
      <MilloraPrivacy lang="en" />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
